# Public release repo (jacob-balslev/skills) — published to https://www.skills.sh/jacob-balslev/skills/
#
# SECURITY / PRIVACY BOUNDARY:
# Only the curated `skills/` tree and governance files may be tracked here. The internal/flat
# skill library (scope: operational, sales-hub-grounded), generated manifests, usage reports,
# and scratch files must NEVER be committed — publishing them would expose internal architecture,
# schema, and file paths to the public marketplace. (See the 2026-05-20 cleanup: 284 flat
# `scope: operational` skills were sitting unpushed and would have published on a `git push`.)
#
# Model: ignore everything at the repo root, then re-include only the known-good public set.
# Re-including the *directory* itself (e.g. `!/skills/`) makes its descendants trackable; this
# avoids the git rule that a file cannot be re-included if its parent directory stays excluded.
# Adding a new top-level file/dir to the public repo requires an explicit allow entry below.
#
# SH-6343 (2026-05-22): the audit loop writes eval artifacts to flat skills
# (skills/<name>/evals/), which `/*` would otherwise ignore. The generated block near
# the bottom of this file (between the `SH-6343` markers) re-includes ONLY the evals/
# tree of each PUBLIC-SAFE flat skill — bodies and operational/Sales-Hub skills stay
# ignored. Never hand-edit that block; regenerate it with
# `node scripts/skill/generate-public-eval-gitignore.js`.
/*
!/.github/
!/.gitignore
!/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/hooks/
!/scripts/
!/skills/

# Belt-and-suspenders: never track secrets, env, or local build artifacts even under allowed dirs.
*.env
*.env.*
*.local
*.log
.DS_Store
node_modules/

# >>> SH-6343 public-safe eval allowlist (generated — do not edit by hand) >>>
# 142 public-safe flat skills — eval artifacts tracked, skill bodies stay ignored.
# Regenerate: node scripts/skill/generate-public-eval-gitignore.js
